# Card files whose DEFAULT SHARE ROOT literal a site deploy script must rewrite.
#
# The card ships working defaults (`/cluster/aba`, cluster "dev-cluster") rather
# than __TOKEN__ placeholders, so a bare deployment renders clean — see
# install/ood/README.md and test_shipped_app_files_carry_no_template_tokens.
# A deployment that roots ABA anywhere else has to rewrite that literal, and
# only in the files below: everywhere else the value arrives through the
# environment.
#
# Paths are relative to install/ood/aba/. Read by the site deploy script; kept
# exact by test_the_site_rewrite_list_is_complete_and_exact, which fails if a
# new file starts depending on the literal and nobody adds it here.
#
# WHY THESE THREE
#   form.yml.erb, submit.yml.erb   render in the DASHBOARD, before any of this
#                                  app's shell has run, so nothing has exported
#                                  ABA_SITE_CONFIG yet and the literal is the
#                                  only thing that resolves site.yaml.
#   template/before.sh.erb         runs FIRST on the node and is where
#                                  ABA_SHARE is defined. Its `${ABA_SHARE:-…}`
#                                  reads like an overridable fallback, but on an
#                                  ordinary OOD launch nothing sets ABA_SHARE
#                                  beforehand (submit.yml.erb does not export
#                                  it), so the literal IS the value. Every other
#                                  template/ script runs after this one and
#                                  takes the root from the environment.
form.yml.erb
submit.yml.erb
template/before.sh.erb
